2. Also verify the re-fetch: the mock `jira_get_ticket` gets called with the TC key; count calls; assert TC key was fetched. And assert that in 'none' mode no TC re-fetch happens (only the bug key fetch).
3. Keep existing tests passing: the existing gh-916 fixtures stuff labels into the stubs — after the fix, in label mode `tracker.getIssue(tc.key)` is called; the mock `jira_get_ticket` returns the BUG ticket regardless of key... wait! In the existing tests:

```js
