jira_get_ticket: function() { return gh916BugTicket(gh916DirectTc('TS-70', 'New', ['stage_passed'])); }
```

The mock ignores args and always returns the bug ticket. After the fix, in label mode `findDirectLinkedTCs` re-fetches `tracker.getIssue('TS-70')` → mock returns the bug ticket again (no issuetype Test Case in fields? gh916BugTicket fields: labels, issuelinks — no issuetype, no status). Then `isBlockingTC(tc)` reads `tc.fields.status` → undefined; `tracker.hasStage(tc, 'PASSED', 'Passed')`: status null; label mode → `_labelNames(ticket.labels || fields.labels || [])` — the bug ticket has `labels: []` → no marker → NOT passed → blocking! The existing test "a TC marked stage_passed is non-blocking — the Bug completes" would FAIL (action = waiting).

