{"content":"# Thread 2 — `checkBugTestsPassed` label-mode gates blind on the direct-links path — FIXED

`findDirectLinkedTCs` (`js/checkBugTestsPassed.js`) now re-fetches every direct-linked TC in full when `tracker.stageFallback() === 'label'`, so `hasStage` sees real `fields.labels` instead of the label-less `issuelinks` stubs Jira returns:

```javascript
if (tracker.stageFallback() === 'label' && tcs.length > 0) {
    return tcs.map(function(tc) {
        try {
            return tracker.getIssue(tc.key) || tc;
        } catch (e) {
            console.warn('Could not re-fetch', tc.key, 'with full fields — falling back to the link stub:', e);
            return tc;
        }
    });
}
return tcs;
```

- Default `'none'` mode keeps the stubs — status-only comparison, zero extra reads (pinned by a test asserting `jira_get_ticket` is called only with the Bug key).
- A failed re-fetch degrades to the stub (check stays conservative — TC keeps blocking), covered by its own test.
- The gh-916 fixtures were rewritten to the realistic shape you called out: the `issuelinks` stub never carries labels; `stage_passed` / `stage_bug_to_fix` exist only on the full re-fetch, and the tests assert the TC key was actually re-fetched.

Suite: `checkBugTestsPassed: stage-label fallback (gh-916)` — 4 tests, red before the fix (both label-mode cases returned `waiting` with the realistic stubs), green after.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_2.md"}

{"content":"# Thread 4 — `stageKeyForStatusName` loses the fallback for configured-status projects — FIXED

Went with the code fix (first option): `stageKeyForStatusName` (`js/smAgent.js`) got a second resolution pass. The first pass (unchanged) matches the configured `jira.statuses` name exactly; when it misses — the renamed-status project you described — a second pass matches the **default (key-derived) status name case-insensitively**, still restricted to `TAG_ONLY_STAGE_KEYS`:

```javascript
var wanted = String(statusName === undefined || statusName === null ? '' : statusName).toLowerCase();
if (wanted) {
    for (var dkey in TAG_ONLY_STAGE_KEYS) {
        if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(TAG_ONLY_STAGE_KEYS, dkey)) continue;
        var derived = configModule.STATUSES[dkey];
        if (derived && String(derived).toLowerCase() === wanted) {
            return dkey;
        }
    }
}
```

So a project with `jira.statuses.READY_FOR_TESTING: 'ReadyForTest'` + `useConfiguredStatusesInQueries: true` keeps the `sm.json` literal `targetStatus: "Ready For Testing"`, and a rejected transition now still lands the `stage_ready_for_testing` marker — which the `{stage.READY_FOR_TESTING:...}` gate resolves through the configured name, so the ticket stays visible to the SM. A rule that already uses the project's own status name keeps matching via the first pass. Dev-flow statuses (`In Development`, …) still resolve to `null` → plain move.

Tests (in `smAgent: targetStatus stage-label fallback (gh-916)`): the literal-`targetStatus` renamed-project case was red before the fix (no marker), green after; the configured-name match and the "unconfigured targetStatus stays a plain move" pins are in place.
